    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Formed around 933 by uniting Upper and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burgundy">Lower Burgundy</a>, it stretched from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-geneva">Lake Geneva</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</li><li>From 1032 it was the third kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, beside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</li><li>Real power lay with counts, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and the houses of Savoy and Viennois; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> gradually absorbed its lands.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 972 Muslim raiders from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fraxinetum">Fraxinetum</a> on the Provençal coast captured Abbot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majolus-of-cluny">Majolus of Cluny</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>; the outrage led to the destruction of their base soon afterwards.</p></aside>
    </section>

